  "rules": [
    "Every new root token is globally unique across project history.",
    "A historical root may never be reassigned to an unrelated identity.",
    "A historical root may be intentionally inherited by a Golden/protocol/verifier/policy identity when lineage is explicit and provenance-preserving.",
    "Derived lineage is not reuse: ARYRA Golden Layout, URSYNEX Golden Finalizer, MUSTAVEX Golden Metadata, CORVEXON Golden Trail, FALCION Golden Cleaning and LUTRAVEX Golden Naming Scheme are intentional inherited authorities.",
    "One semantic version has one normalized release codename prospectively; historical anomalies are preserved rather than rewritten.",
    "One release codename identifies one normalized semantic version prospectively; superseded naming artifacts remain recorded with status.",
    "Correction/build labels do not create a second release identity.",
    "Every assigned root enters the permanent reserved registry immediately.",
    "Before assignment, candidates are checked against CHANGELOG registry, package/documentation tokens and Library/file-name history.",
    "Release codenames use an original Latin animal root plus an approved Bakugan-like synthetic suffix family.",
    "Prospective semantic releases rotate suffix families; the current family must differ from each of the three immediately prior semantic-release families."
  ],
